{"timestamp": 1779427050.1179738, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I found Alice dead in weapons. It looks like Eve is also dead, though I didn't see her body. \n\nMy route this round was lower engine -> upper engine -> oxygen -> medbay -> electrical -> security -> weapons. I saw Diana a few times along the way. She was near me in medbay and electrical, and right before I went into weapons, I saw her leaving security to go down to navigation. Because of that timing, I highly doubt Diana is the duck. \n\nI haven't seen Charlie or Frank the entire round. Since Diana is mostly cleared in my eyes for Alice's death, it has to be one of you two. Where were you, and did either of you see what happened to Eve?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779427077.1493871, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I started around medbay, went electrical, then security/weapons side, down through nav and storage, and ended in lower engine. I did see Alice in weapons earlier, alive, but that was not right before the report \u2014 I left that side after passing through.\n\nFor Eve: I saw her in electrical early, and then near lower engine late. Frank was also in lower engine around that time. I didn\u2019t see Eve\u2019s body before the report got called, but if Eve died in/near lower engine, Frank is the person I\u2019d want to hear from because he was right there with her at the end.\n\nBob, your Alice find could still technically be a self-report, but Diana being around your route makes that less likely. Between the two deaths, Frank has the strongest connection to Eve from what I saw."}}
{"timestamp": 1779427095.3322747, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Charlie is trying to frame me by twisting the truth. \n\nMy route was security -> navigation -> storage -> lower engine, and I ended up in upper engine. It is true that I was in lower engine late in the round, but Charlie conveniently left out a crucial detail: **he was there too.** \n\nRight around tick 17, I was in lower engine. I saw Eve enter from upper engine, and at the exact same time, Charlie entered from storage. After seeing both of them, I left and went up to upper engine to do my task. That means I left Charlie alone with Eve. If Eve died in lower engine right at the end of the round, Charlie is the one who did it after I walked away. \n\nThis fits perfectly with Bob's report. Charlie admitted he was in weapons with Alice earlier. The Duck's kill cooldown would give Charlie enough time to kill Alice in weapons early on, travel down through nav and storage (which matches his claimed route and where I saw him coming from), and then kill Eve in lower engine right before Bob found Alice's body. \n\nCharlie is the Duck. He tried to get ahead of the Eve kill by throwing suspicion on me because he knew I saw him walk into lower engine with her. Diana, you're up next, but I'm voting Charlie."}}
{"timestamp": 1779427126.478678, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Bob, I can completely vouch for you. Our routes basically synced up perfectly \u2014 I saw you enter Medbay at tick 10, we were both in Electrical around tick 14, and you came into Security at tick 19 right before the report. Since we were constantly crossing paths and you easily could have killed me but didn't, I know for a fact neither of us is the Duck. \n\nThat means it is 100% between Charlie and Frank. And honestly, Frank's logic is completely airtight. \n\nCharlie, you admitted to being in Weapons (where Alice was found), and you admitted to being in Lower Engine (where Eve was). It's incredibly suspicious that you just happened to be at both likely crime scenes while trying to casually brush it off. On top of that, Frank caught you omitting the crucial fact that he left you completely alone with Eve in Lower Engine right at the end of the round. \n\nMy own observations back Frank up, too. I saw Eve leaving Medbay and heading towards Upper Engine at tick 8, which perfectly matches Frank's story of seeing her enter Lower Engine from the top side later on. Charlie's story relies on convenient omissions and pointing fingers at the guy who actually saw him with the victim. \n\nBob, Frank, we have this locked down. Charlie is the Duck. I'm voting for Charlie."}}
{"timestamp": 1779427138.4108768, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Charlie"}}
{"timestamp": 1779427228.3553116, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Frank is making one big assumption and then treating it like proof: that he \u201cleft me alone\u201d with Eve. I never hid that he was there \u2014 I literally said Frank was in lower engine with Eve late. That was the whole point.\n\nFrom my perspective, I entered lower engine from storage and saw Eve come in from upper engine, with Frank already there. Frank says he left upward, but that is just his word. If Eve died there, Frank had the exact same access and timing, and he\u2019s the one trying hardest to make the timeline sound locked before anyone questions it.\n\nAlso, on Alice: I saw Alice alive in Weapons earlier and left that side. Frank claims a route starting near Security/Nav/Storage, which is right next to Weapons/Security. He had just as much opportunity to be on that side and then end up storage/lower engine. Bob and Diana only clear each other \u2014 they do not clear Frank.\n\nFrank is pushing \u201cCharlie was at both places\u201d because it sounds clean, but the actual shared point is lower engine, where Frank was also present with Eve. I think Frank killed Eve and is using the fact that he saw me enter to frame me before I can point it out. My vote is Frank."}}
